opt bounded commitment.','A2':'Election, term dispatch and transfer establish or withdraw leader authority.','A3':'Snapshot catch-up and storage restart recover committed history and membership.','A4':'Applied configuration controls eligibility and joint-majority obligations.','A5':'Ready and completion accounting separate commit, issued application and completed application.','A6':'Library emits ordered persistence work; caller supplies durable storage; in-repository MemoryStorage and acknowledgment mechanics are implemented here.','A7':'Node/RawNode expose proposals and correlated read states; caller supplies ticks, transport, state machine and retries.'}\nmap={'version':1,'target_profile':{'system_boundary':'Captured go.etcd.io/raft/v3 library including RawNode/Node, log, tracker, configuration and MemoryStorage. Embedding transport, durable medium and state machine are external interfaces; their in-library coordination remains in scope.','protocol_contexts':['Node identity, election term, per-node role, ordered log index, applied voter configuration','Crash-fault assumptions with caller-compliant persistence and message production; no Byzantine fabricated messages'], 'external_interfaces':['Storage','RawNode Ready/Advance or AsyncStorageWrites messages','Node Step/Tick/ApplyConfChange/Stop'], 'ownership':['RawNode is thread-unsafe and serialized by caller; Node owns a channel-select loop.','Application owns storage persistence, state-machine execution, configuration application and transport.'], 'variants':['Ordinary Ready/Advance','AsyncStorageWrites','PreVote/CheckQuorum','Joint explicit and automatic transitions'], 'source_ids':['S-raw-api','S-node-loop','S-caller','S-async','S-storage']},'activities':[dict(class_id=k,applicability='applicable',purpose=v['relation'],realization_summary=summaries[k],source_ids=sorted(set(s for b in B if b['primary_activity']==k for s in b['source_ids']))) for k,v in roles.items()],'behaviors':B,'facts':facts,'surfaces':[dict(entry_point='raft.appliedTo / tickHeartbeat transfer timeout',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-auto','B-transfer','B-apply'],reason='Can transfer rejection consume the last required automatic-exit trigger with no later application completion?',source_ids=['S-application','S-timeout','S-ready'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='raft.switchToConfig / releasePendingReadIndexMessages',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-config','B-client'],reason='Does changed-quorum commitment leave pending requests behind, and what responsibility remains given the explicit caller retry contract?',source_ids=['S-config','S-read-release','S-client-read'],high_consequence=False)],'core_overview':{'status':'usable','formation':{'explanation':'A1: a leader assigns term/index to proposals, appends unstable entries and replicates through peer Progress. Local and remote append support is published after persistence. Responses pass term dispatch and known-peer checks, update Match and contribute only through current configured voter majorities; joint commitment is the minimum of the two majority-supported indexes. maybeCommit advances only when that index has current term. Advancement broadcasts to followers; matching append constrains follower commit to received prefix, heartbeat producer caps it by peer Match, and committed conflicts cannot overwrite history. Ready exposes committed entries with applying cursor and size controls; caller applies configurations and state-machine entries, then completion updates applied. Rejected appends backtrack; heartbeat responses reopen flow and snapshots catch up compacted peers.','behavior_ids':['B-form','B-follower','B-io','B-apply','B-recover'],'fact_ids':['F-commit','F-applied'],'source_ids':['S-replication','S-log-qualification','S-majority','S-joint','S-follower','S-send','S-ready','S-log-apply']},'context':{'explanation':'A2: eligible voters campaign only without unapplied committed configuration or pending snapshot. Real campaign increments term, records self vote durably and requests votes using last log term/index; configured majority votes acquire leadership. Pre-vote preserves local term until its quorum succeeds. Leader acquisition resets volatile support and appends a current-term empty entry. Higher terms normally step down with lease/pre-vote exceptions; old replies are discarded. Quorum loss can step down; transfer selects a caught-up voter, drops proposals while active and expires after electionTimeout if still leader. Restart restores HardState/configuration and enters follower. Existing committed decisions remain valid across authority changes; old storage snapshots and term-independent application completion remain consumable, while entry-stability acknowledgment requires matching generation.','behavior_ids':['B-election','B-transfer','B-io','B-recover'],'fact_ids':['F-authority','F-config','F-commit'],'source_ids':['S-election','S-authority','S-dispatch','S-transfer','S-timeout','S-init','S-storage-resp']},'connection':{'explanation':'Applied membership determines support eligibility for both election and log commitment. Joint config requires both old and new majorities; recovery restores that same configuration, not a fresh quorum. Term reset clears votes and peer progress but retains committed history; log freshness and committed-prefix guards constrain subsequent formation. The new leader conservatively sets pendingConfIndex to inherited last index. Config proposals cannot overtake unapplied changes under normal validation. Automatic joint exit depends on application completion and leader role, and uses ordinary proposal admission, so an active transfer can reject it. Ordinary Ready completion only issues an apply acknowledgment for nonempty committed entries. readOnly support resets with authority, while pending pre-current-term reads have a distinct release path; their cross-context details remain open and their external API assigns retries to callers.','behavior_ids':['B-config','B-auto','B-election','B-form','B-apply','B-client'],'fact_ids':['F-config','F-applied','F-authority','F-commit'],'source_ids':['S-config','S-config-change','S-election','S-authority','S-application','S-proposal','S-ready','S-client-read']},'core_gaps':[],'open_details':['Automatic exit after failed transfer with no new application completion.','Configuration-driven pending-read release and pendingReadIndexMessages across terms; caller retries constrain obligations.','Fine-grained asynchronous snapshot/application overlap and resource-error recovery.'],'rationale':'Representative formation, authority, membership, persistence, rejection/retry, recovery and consumption paths are traced. Local questions remain; this map does not imply comprehensive safety or API coverage.'}}\nq={'question':'When application completion attempts automatic joint exit during a leadership transfer that later times out, does the implementation resume the selected automatic transition without requiring an unrelated client proposal?','importance':'A joint configuration left indefinitely can retain outgoing quorum requirements and block subsequent reconfiguration despite sufficient members being available; this is a scoped progress concern, not an established consensus-safety violation.','source_ids':['S-auto-contract','S-application','S-proposal','S-timeout','S-abort','S-ready','S-advance','S-auto-test','S-node-loop'],'participants':['Leader','Transferee voter','Other voters','Embedding application'],'objects':['Active joint configuration with AutoLeave','Empty leave-joint log proposal','Ready application completion'],'contexts':['Serialized ordinary RawNode Ready/Advance','Leader remains in same term after unsuccessful transfer','Quiet client workload with required ticks and Ready processing continuing'],'event_paths':['Commit and apply automatic joint-entry configuration','Start transfer before corresponding application completion acknowledgment','Advance while transfer active rejects automatic exit proposal','Transfer timeout clears leadTransferee; continue ticks, actual network messages and Ready handling'],'activity_classes':['A4','A1','A2'],'fact_ids':['F-config'],'behavior_ids':['B-config','B-auto','B-recover'],'supporting_behavior_ids':{'B-transfer':'Supplies proposal suppression and timeout clearing.','B-apply':'Determines whether subsequent Ready completion invokes appliedTo.','B-io':'Defines legal persistence/completion order.','B-election':'Alternative successful-transfer/new-leader empty-entry application can restore the trigger.','B-form':'Exit proposal follows ordinary replicated commitment.'},'obligation_relation_kind':'consumption','counterevidence':['AutoLeave retry occurs on each later applied entry; new leader empty-entry application can trigger it.','Existing TestRawNodeJointAutoLeave exercises leadership loss and reacquisition.','Transfer can succeed rather than timeout; a pending committed entry could independently supply the missing trigger.'],'unknowns':['Can a legal history commit joint entry and start transfer before Advance without forcing another application completion later?','Do any caller obligations require new proposals or another trigger after a failed transfer, beyond ticks and Ready processing?','Can all in-flight appends, callbacks and queues be accounted for in a quiet suffix, rather than mistaking finite waiting for lost continuation?'],'trigger_rationale':'The appliedTo retry comment assumes another advance, but Advance creates application completion only for nonempty committed entries; transfer timeout clears a field without scheduling a retry. This concrete producer/consumer mismatch motivates checking legal history before a formal obligation. Contract reading and existing alternative new-leader path do not settle the same-leader quiet suffix. The separate pending-read question has weaker completion authority because retries are explicitly caller-owned.','disposition':'needs_specific_evidence','preferred_check':'controlled_schedule'}\nsubmission={'action':'continue','rationale':'Record usable initial two-core map and select sourced automatic configuration-transition retry question, retaining independent limits and counterevidence.','sources':sources,'map_path':'map.json','question':q,'feedback':{'ref_ids':['S-client-read','S-ready','S-auto-test','S-election','S-follower','S-restore'],'answered':'Completed the representative backbone and mapped acquired learning. The suspected missing pending-read release in switchToConfig is not by itself a completion defect: Node.ReadIndex explicitly permits loss and requires caller retry. Automatic joint exit has a separate implementation-owned when-possible contract. Existing auto-leave test covers leadership loss/reacquisition, while RawNode Advance only generates an application response for nonempty committed entries, preserving the failed-transfer quiet-suffix question.','remaining':q['unknowns'],'understanding':'updated','rationale':'Separate documented caller retry from automatic configuration duty; preserve the unsuccessful-transfer discriminator rather than expanding guard-only tests.'}}\nopen('map.json','w').write(json.dumps(map,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nopen('submission.json','w').write(json.dumps(submission,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 build_map.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-05_08-31-36-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": false, \"run_id\": \"e341bd5385004f23a51456f52bf58029\", \"audit_spec_version\": 0, \"elapsed_seconds\": 145.336945534, \"diagnostics\": [{\"details\": {\"blocked_checks\": \"Checks requiring this excerpt await valid source bytes\"}, \"code\": \"source_range\", \"category\": \"material\", \"task\": \"\",